// F128.log(x, base) is correctly rounded: ln x / ln base rounded once to nearest-even, checked against mpmath (400
// bits, 2000 where the quotient lies within 2^-370 of a midpoint) for random pairs over the whole range, every
// kind of hard case (both near 1, exact powers such as log(8, 2) = 3, subnormals, the ends of the range, x = base),
// and the pairs whose fast-tier quotient can't be rounded, which also run through the F128Big tier alone. Near 1 the
// quotient can sit very close to a midpoint: log(1 - 2^-112, 1 + 2^-110) is within 2^-334 of one. The special cases
// keep the F128 quotient of the two logarithms.

import Standard::Format
import Standard::Os

